<pre class="metadata">
Title: IdP Registration API
Shortname: idp-registration
Level: None
Status: CG-DRAFT
Group: fedidcg
Repository: w3c-fedid/idp-registration
URL: https://w3c-fedid.github.io/idp-registration/
Editor: Sam Goto, w3cid 50308, Google Inc. https://google.com, goto@google.com
Abstract: This specification extends the Federated Credential Management API [[FEDCM]] so that
    the user agent can remember the user's handles (e.g. <code>@alice.example</code>,
    <code>alice@social.example</code> or <code>https://alice.example</code>) and the identity
    providers they resolve to, and so that relying parties can request <em>any</em> of them that
    speaks a protocol they accept, instead of enumerating identity providers. A handle is
    registered either by the identity provider, with the user's permission, or by the user typing
    it.
